  "body": "Ports the gate and the decision collection into one cross-platform Rust tool, `cargo xtask`. Part of #748; the release port is split out to #749.\n\n## What changed\n- **New workspace member `xtask/`** (`publish = false`; alias `xtask = \"run -p xtask --\"` in `.cargo/config.toml`). 8 files, each under 300 lines, each with a provenance line. No `unwrap`/`expect`/`panic!` outside tests.\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick [--base main] [--heavy] | batch | release | test <filter> [--crate c] [--binary b] [--exact]`, and `--dry-run` (alias `--plan`) on any of them.\n  - `cargo xtask decisions --version X.Y.Z`: the same output as collect-decisions.ps1, and it now rejects a version that isn't `X.Y.Z`.\n- **It reproduces `gate.ps1`, not `gate.sh`.** That covers SLOW_BINARIES, the BATCH/ALL/SHARED/CLIPPY lists, `-j 6` / `--test-threads=6`, the ui CWD `crates/ui`, and quick's diff-to-test selection (changed `#[test]` fns run `--exact`; changed heavy fns are build-only unless `--heavy`; a suite edited outside its fns, or a new suite, runs whole; a src module runs the suites whose gate map names it, by submodule first; shared test input runs the crate's suites; geometry/cl/Cargo/.cargo/toolchain fall back to batch). It also covers the `gate-logs/<tier>-<timestamp>/` per-step logs, the failing-suite note, the summary table and the exit code. The gate drives `cargo test` / `cargo clippy` only and never launches or globs a test executable.\n- **Wrappers.** `scripts/gate.ps1` (`-Tier`, `-Base`, `-Test`, `-Crate`, `-Binary`, `-Exact`, `-Heavy`, `-DryRun`), `scripts/gate.sh` (`quick [base]`, `batch`, `release`, `test <name> [crate] [--exact]`, `DRY_RUN=1`) and `scripts/collect-decisions.{ps1,sh}` are now thin forwarders. gate.sh accepts `--ignored` and drops it, because the gate reads `#[ignore]` from the source.\n- **Process text.** AGENTS.md (\"Three gate tiers\", Actions budget, \"Test the change\", SLOW_BINARIES, release step 2, the decisions ledger, and the fork process-file list, which gains `xtask/` and `.cargo/config.toml`), the gate-runner and PR-reviewer agents, the review-prs / resolve-conflicts / work-issue skills, README and docs/decisions/README now name `cargo xtask gate ...` as the one command and say the wrappers still work. A fork whose tag predates xtask also adds the `\"xtask\"` member line in its sync commit; the AGENTS.md fork-sync text says so.\n- **`.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 6 -> 7.** Not announced on #681: the merging session does that.\n- **Decisions:** `docs/decisions/748-xtask-gate.md`.\n\n**Deliberate differences from gate.ps1** (details in the decisions file):\n1. `-Test` on a fn in a `tests/` module under `src/` (e.g. `ui/src/egui_app/tests/layout.rs`) was planned as `--test layout`, a suite that doesn't exist. It now runs as `--lib`.\n2. Several lib files matching one filter gave duplicate `--lib` steps. They now share one step.\n3. The heavy-fn hint text names `--heavy` / `gate test <name>`.\n4. A change under `xtask/` runs xtask's unit tests in quick.\n5. The log-dir timestamp is UTC.\n6. Hashtable-ordered groups are now sorted.\n\n**New dependency (for `needs-maintainer`):** `regex = \"1\"` in xtask only. It is already in `Cargo.lock` (pulled in by tracing-subscriber's env-filter), so no new crate enters the tree; the lock gains only the `xtask` package entry. It lets the gate-map, test-fn-span and diff-hunk patterns port one-for-one from gate.ps1's .NET regexes. serde_json isn't needed, because there's no artifact list to parse (the gate never runs test exes itself).\n\n**Release: not ported.** `scripts/release.ps1` (243 lines, 10 phases, zip + installer + signing) stays as it is. Follow-up: #749 (\"xtask release: port scripts/release.ps1 cross-platform\", Part of #748). That's why this PR says `Refs #748`, not `Fixes`.\n\n## How tested (Windows 11 only)\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 13 unit tests pass. They pin the plan selection on a throwaway fixture workspace (changed files -> planned steps):\n  - `changed_test_fn_runs_exact_and_heavy_fn_only_builds`\n  - `suite_edit_outside_fns_and_new_suite_run_whole`\n  - `src_module_maps_to_gate_mapped_suites`\n  - `shared_test_input_runs_every_suite_of_the_crate`\n  - `manifest_or_shared_crate_falls_back_to_batch`\n  - `nothing_in_crates_plans_nothing_and_xtask_runs_its_own_tests`\n  - `batch_skips_slow_binaries_and_release_runs_everything`\n  - `slow_list_is_pinned`\n  - `single_test_finds_suite_and_lib_fns`\n  - `test_fn_spans_cover_attrs_through_closing_brace`\n  - `cli_parses_the_gate_forms`\n  - `decisions_gathered_in_issue_order_and_removed`\n  - `log_names_stamps_and_notes_match_the_old_script`\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- **Parity, `--dry-run` against origin/main's `scripts/gate.ps1 -DryRun`, same tree.** The summary/wall lines were stripped and the outputs diffed.\n  - `batch`: **identical** (31 lines).\n  - `release`: **identical** (43 lines).\n  - `quick` on a 6-file sample diff (a scratch worktree at origin/main): one changed fn in `app/tests/arcs.rs`, one changed `#[ignore]`d fn in `app/tests/operations.rs`, `app/src/posting.rs`, `motion/src/machining2d/arcs.rs`, the header line of `sim/tests/arc_plane.rs`, and a new untracked `tools/tests/parity_new.rs`. Result: 6 steps, all identical (tools new suite; sim whole suite; motion `--lib` + 33 gate-mapped suites; app `--lib` + 81 gate-mapped suites; app build-only `operations`; app `arcs` 1 fn `--exact`) and all plan notes identical. The only differences: git's CRLF warnings, which the old script let through, and the reworded `--heavy` hint (item 3 above).\n  - `-Test` forms: identical for `fitted_arcs_recover_a_bore_rim -Exact`, `the_ramp_flag -Crate app` (ignored -> release), `tool_kind -Crate tools`, `-Binary nope` (no match, exit 1) and `structural`. `the_viewport_tab_is_permanent -Exact` differs on purpose (item 1): old `--test layout` (no such suite), new `--lib`.\n  - Wrappers: `gate.ps1 -Tier batch -DryRun` gives output identical to `cargo xtask gate batch --dry-run`. `gate.ps1 -Test ... -Crate tools -Exact -DryRun`, `DRY_RUN=1 gate.sh test ... tools --exact`, `gate.sh release` (13 steps) and `gate.sh quick origin/main` produce the expected plans. `collect-decisions.sh 1.2` is refused (exit 2).\n- **Real run end to end:** `cargo xtask gate test tools_bin_lists_a_sane_catalog --crate tools --exact` built and ran `camcraft-tools --test headless_bin -- --exact ...`: 1 passed, log written, summary printed, exit 0.\n\n## Not exercised\n- **macOS and Linux were not exercised**: this machine runs Windows only. The code uses `Path`/`PathBuf`, `CARGO` from the environment, and no `.exe` or drive assumptions, and `gate.sh` is plain bash 3.2. It still needs one run on each OS.\n- A real `quick`/`batch`/`release` run (only dry runs plus the one real test step). This PR's own quick falls back to batch (manifest change), and a full batch wasn't run, as briefed.\n- `cargo xtask decisions` against the real `docs/decisions/` (it would consume the files). The fixture unit test covers it.\n\nChangelog: none (process/tooling)\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #748\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
